A||||4||saleenfiero||Brakes screwed, what now??!?||||8||
Z||000000||saleenfiero||05-03-2001||08:00 PM||||Had the car looked at today, couldn't tighten the e-brake EQ any more, so I thought I'd take it to a shop.  Got the answer:  machanic couldn't adjust it either=seized caliper.  Now, I want the grand am brake setup, but I can't do it myself and feel kind of stupid trying to describe any little nuances to installing the g-am rotors and calipers.  Is the install identical to simple replacement of fiero calipers?  Should I maybe just stick with stock fiero parts or what?||||reg||8
Z||000001||PBJ||05-03-2001||08:12 PM||||I have done the G/AM brake conversion to my wife's 86. and what a differance.  I feel no noticable brake fad-press the pedal and it seems the brakes work better as you are stopping.  If you are going to do it remember: no more park brake-so you can't get it saftied/certified like this.  Only do it if you do it completely-NO frts now and rears later.  It also cost me $300.00 cdn in parts alone-I did not return any core(s).  I got my info from going to <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroproject.com</A>  then went to links and selected fiero secrets,  you will find all kinds of ideas.||||reg||14
Z||000002||theogre||05-03-2001||11:25 PM||||You could not pay me to put GA brakes on the rear. Especially if you are not doing the front at the same time. read in my cave... <A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Ogre's Fiero Cave</A> Before you even think of this you need to check your inspection requirements very thuroughly.<P>You can get rebuilt calipers from autozone for about $30 each. I don't know if you can shop them online or if they ship to canada... autozone.com <P>I'm told You can buy a rebuild kit from GM that includes parts for both calipers. GM # 18019027<P>If Canada had the same rear brake recall on 84-86 Fiero as the U.S.... You might can make GM do the work for free if the recall was not done. The U.S. recall data/links are in my cave. I don't have GM Canada's id code for it. In the U.S. this recall ONLY applies to 84-86 manual tranny cars.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 05-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jake_Dragon||05-04-2001||07:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<B><BR>You can get rebuilt calipers from autozone for about $30 each.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I just replaced my rear calipers with rebuilt ones from Autozone and they ran $45 if you go that way make sure you have everything you need before you leave the store. Like the pesky little clip that holds your pad to the caliper.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/rebel33/dragon.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||05-04-2001||08:41 PM||||That's still better than what most others want for them. Maybe it varies by region a bit...<P>It always pays to shop around. I just put on rear rotors for about $30 each. Most others want $50+ each.||||reg||1
